   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food security</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">DFAT&#x2019;s Disaster Resilience Program (DRP) strengthened climate resilient agriculture and improved food security through grant funding provided to Fijian CSO, the Foundation for Rural Integrated Enterprises and Development (FRIEND). 
&#x200d;
In the last year, DRP supported 1543 people (60 per cent female and 5 per cent people with disability) in 31 communities to improve food security and climate resilient agriculture practices. Through grant funding from the DRP, FRIEND carried out trainings on climate smart farming techniques which built on traditional farming knowledge. FRIEND also distributed seeds and farming equipment to support households and communities to re-establish and grow their farms following significant flooding.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved Governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">DFAT&#x2019;s Disaster Resilience Program (DRP) supports humanitarian preparedness and disaster risk reduction in Fiji, including by partnering with humanitarian Civil Society Organisations (CSOs) to strengthen their institutional capacity. During the reporting period, DFAT supported Medical Services Pacific (MSP) to improve governance structures by developing and implementing a Disaster Management Plan and a Strategic Plan. The Disaster Management Plan established clear protocols for managing emergency preparedness and response, outlining decision-making processes and staff responsibilities. The Strategic Plan set MSP&#x2019;s organisational values as well as specific governance objectives, including transparency and financial sustainability. 
&#x200d;
DRP also provided Gender Equality and Disability and Social Inclusion (GEDSI) support throughout the development of these plans. The Disaster Management Plan includes GEDSI training recommendations for MSP personnel involved in emergency responses, GEDSI considerations for funding proposals to support MSP&#x2019;s emergency response efforts, and standard GEDSI indicators to report on. A core value documented in MSP&#x2019;s Strategic Plan is inclusion, committing the organisation to ensure their services are accessible to all.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
